150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 54 0 R
/T (A web page is a document that integrates structured HTML, text, links, media and metadata. I open one of my files, the browser reads the HTML from beginning to end, generates a Document Object Model, and translates each element and shows the structure. It also follows the references including the three local image paths. This assignment does not use any CSS or JavaScript. Used semantic tags in specific locations. However, in the index.html file, the store introduction and contact details are on the main since they are the unique content of the page, while the customer information is an aside since it supplements the introduction. The material-selection guidance in products.html relies on the term article as the advice is self-explanatory. The request controls are located in order.html, inside form and fieldset, which provide more meaningful descriptions of what they're used for than div elements. The Submit button today will not save or place an order at the shop. This form uses GET, and is pointed to by order.html, so the browser validates the required fields, encodes the names and values of those fields into a query string, and reopens order.html. This action can be replaced in a subsequent assignment with a real server endpoint.)
/E (A web page is a document that integrates structured HTML, text, links, media and metadata. I open one of my files, the browser reads the HTML from beginning to end, generates a Document Object Model, and translates each element and shows the structure. It also follows the references including the three local image paths. This assignment does not use any CSS or JavaScript. Used semantic tags in specific locations. However, in the index.html file, the store introduction and contact details are on the main since they are the unique content of the page, while the customer information is an aside since it supplements the introduction. The material-selection guidance in products.html relies on the term article as the advice is self-explanatory. The request controls are located in order.html, inside form and fieldset, which provide more meaningful descriptions of what they're used for than div elements. The Submit button today will not save or place an order at the shop. This form uses GET, and is pointed to by order.html, so the browser validates the required fields, encodes the names and values of those fields into a query string, and reopens order.html. This action can be replaced in a subsequent assignment with a real server endpoint.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
